--- Iteration 1 / 8 ---
Phase 0 complete. Key findings:

**Trial retention** (~93% at 12mo in PURPOSE 1) is a ceiling, not a forecast. The best structural comparator — **cabotegravir (CAB-LA) real-world in the US** — shows **72-75% at 12 months**, a ~20pp drop from trial conditions. Oral PrEP in SSA retains only **50-65% at 12 months** (meta-analysis pooled discontinuation 47.5% in SSA).

**Critical gap: No real-world LEN retention data exists yet.** As of Sep 2026, ~66,000 people have been initiated across 9 African countries (191,620 doses delivered), but the earliest cohorts (Zambia/Eswatini Dec 2025) are only just reaching their 6-month return window. No second-dose return rates have been published. Supply constraints (Gilead manufacturing) may force discontinuation independent of patient willingness — Mozambique is already seeing uptake decline due to limited drug availability, and South Africa has reserved 10,000 doses specifically for returning clients.

The twice-yearly dosing advantage (2 visits/year vs 6 for CAB-LA vs 12+ for oral) is the strongest theoretical argument for higher retention, but it remains empirically unproven at scale.

STOP — one phase per iteration.

